#: ../../libraries/create.rst:2 d05312395a77460a876795de02eed378
msgid "Creating a library"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:4 d0e160489a59479b8d382999655f67bf
msgid ""
"A library is a model - an IBM TS3500, an STK SL500 - with a number of "
"drives, a number of slots, and cartridges of a generation those drives "
"can load. The console only offers combinations MHVTL can really emulate, "
"so a library it lets you build is one that will work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:14 66dce4d499284ee38599df86eaad31f7
msgid "In the console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:16 a7dda83864854c009d42f2e55993c7b8
msgid "**Libraries → Create Library**, at ``/libraries/setup/``. Two ways in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:18 56551c706fde40cb8f403f3717dbdcb3
msgid "Create Library: choose a vendor, or start from the tape"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:22 0c723e02f2904788a86410428a8763a5
msgid "**From a vendor** (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:23 ca0e6b04f7a84aeb827cac9d19dc4df0
msgid ""
"Pick a vendor, then a model. The drive list then shows only the drives "
"that model takes, with its default chosen; the media list only the "
"cartridges that drive writes. The limits on drives, slots and MAP slots "
"are the model's own."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:28 e644ffea6c684a63a6479b07d580383a
msgid "**From the tape**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:29 fb2aa0745b9d46668e0b45bce46b9db0
msgid ""
"If you know which cartridge you need, say so first: **Show vendors whose "
"libraries can take** leaves only the vendors that can, and carries the "
"choice into the form. Choosing ``LTO10`` gets you a model with an "
"``ULT3580-TDA`` drive, ``LTO10`` media and barcodes ending ``LA``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:34 c0ec78cabbde40e1984a34c317ed4852
msgid ""
"Then set how many drives, how many slots, and how many empty slots to "
"leave for tapes added later. Four empty slots is the default; a library "
"with none cannot take a new tape without being reconfigured."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:38 4b75357d31624e4bb2e9acc18ca5370c
msgid "The library form: model, drives, media and slots"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:42 ffa19b95c099457b9ff64b26530fd86f
msgid ""
"Press **Create**. The console writes ``device.conf`` and "
"``library_contents.<id>``, starts the daemons, and creates the tape "
"files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:46 4ff0c4d45b9a40e4aa2c0d67f0a66b44
msgid "From the terminal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../libraries/create.rst:60 c3812c9cba104fb796e644e104ea07d2
msgid ""
"Each step is reported, and a failure says which step failed and leaves "
"the configuration as it was."
msgstr ""

